SWEET IOSurface values, use counts, purgeable (patch 0290, rule 7 sweep after 0289, user 2026-11-10): the IOSurfaceRootUserClient answered SetValue (sel 9), SetPurgeable (sel 20) and the use-count traps (0/1) with zeroed success / no-ops, so IOSurfaceCopyValue/CopyAllValues were empty in every process (CA::Render::Surface::encode ships them to backboardd: colour space, ICC profile, HDR keys) and IOSurfaceIsInUse was always false. Protocol from IOSurface.framework (research 134 s.2/s.3/s.6). Now: per-surface OSDictionary values; sel 9 SetValue ([value,key] or [dict], binary serialized after an 8-byte header; reply u32 generation (old+2)|1), sel 10 UpdateNonBulkValueCache ([u32 0][u32 gen][OSSerializeBinary dict], 0xe00002db when the buffer is small), sel 11 RemoveValue (empty key = all); state page +0x20 generation, +0x28 serialized size. Traps 0/1 = per-client hold of use category 0/1 (the client calls them on its own 0->1 / 1->0), published at state page +0x18/+0x1c, dropped with the client's reference (release or exit). Sel 20 returns the previous purgeable state, stores 0/1, never purges (Empty is kept Volatile with a GAP). Large replies arrive as an unwired client memory descriptor: every descriptor write goes through prepare() + writeBytes + complete() (the first build panicked "IOGMD: not wired for the IODMACommand" in gputest-root1; sweet_struct_out had the same latent bug). No hardware access.

